hadiths[114]{hadithnumber,text}:
"6406","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, narrates: I heard the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, say: \""Among the people, I am the closest to the son of Maryam. All the Prophets are paternal brothers, but there is no Prophet between me and him.\""The narrator says: Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, also used to narrate: The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said: \""The example of me and the other Prophets is like a building which has been beautifully cons"
"6407","The similitude of mine and that of the Apostles (before me) is that of a person who constructed a building and he built it fine and well and the people went round it saying: Never have we seen a building more imposing than this. but for one brick, and I am that brick (with which you give the finishing touch to the building). (Using translation from Muslim 2286a)"
"6408","I am holding people by their sides (saying), 'Come towards Paradise and save yourselves from Hell,' but they are trying to fall into it."
"6409","I moved my camel and started walking ahead of the people. I feared that perhaps some command of the Qur'an might be revealed about me. While I was in this state, I heard someone calling me in a loud voice. I came to the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) and greeted him with salam. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Last night, a surah was revealed to me which is more beloved to me than anything upon which the sun rises (i.e., more beloved than the whole world). Then he recited this verse: ""Indeed, We have given you a clear conquest, that Allah may forgive for you your past and future sins."
"6410","""While the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was returning from Al-Hudaibiyyah it was revealed to him, 'That Allah may forgive you your sins of the past and the future (48:2).' So the Prophet ﷺ said: 'An Ayah has been revealed to me which is dearer to me than whatever is upon the earth.' Then the Prophet ﷺ recited it for them and they said: 'Congratulations O Messenger of Allah! Allah has explained what He will do with you, but what will He do with us?' So (the following) was revealed: 'That He may admit the believing men and the believing women into Gardens under which rivers flow' up to (His Saying) 'a supreme success (48:5).'"" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 3263)"
"6411","I said, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! You recite this supplication frequently, whereas before you did not use to recite it."" So the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""My Lord has informed me that He will soon show me a sign regarding my Ummah. He has commanded me that when I see this sign, I should glorify Him, praise Him, and seek forgiveness from Him. So I have seen that thing."" (That is this verse:) ""When the help of Allah comes and..."" By this is meant the conquest of Makkah."
"6412","I saw the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) that whenever he performed prayer, he would definitely recite: ""So glory be to Allah, praise is exclusively for You, O Allah, forgive me."
"6413","I am not like you. I spend the night in such a state that my Lord gives me food and drink."
"6414","I would have continued to observe continuous fasting for such a period that those who exert themselves excessively would abandon their excessiveness. I spend such time that my Lord gives me food and gives me drink."
"6415","I hope it would have lasted for a longer time."
"6416","The people asked, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Is there one with you as well?"" The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There is one with me as well, but Allah Almighty helped me against him and he became a Muslim."" (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) The narrator has reported this word in the accusative case exactly as it is."
"6417","There is none amongst you with whom is not an attache from amongst the jinn (devil). They (the Companions) said: Messenger of Allah, with you too? Thereupon he said: Yes, but Allah helps me against him and so I am safe from his hand and he does not command me but for good. (Using translation from Muslim 2814a)"
"6418","I seized him and strangled him, until I felt the coolness of his tongue on the back of my hand. If it were not for the supplication of my brother, Sayyiduna Sulaiman (peace be upon him), that came to my mind, that Satan would have been tied up until morning and you people would have seen him."
"6419","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then I remembered the statement of my brother, Sayyiduna Sulaiman (peace be upon him): 'My Lord, forgive me and grant me a kingdom such as will not belong to anyone after me.' The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: So Allah made that devil return in disgrace."
"6420","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I hope that Allah Almighty also granted him this third thing."
"6421","The Prophet ﷺ said, ""I was granted victory with As-Saba and the nation of 'Ad was destroyed by Ad- Dabur (westerly wind) . (Using translation from Bukhārī 1035)"
"6422","""There are four things which the Prophet never gave up: Fasting 'Ashura', (fasting during) the ten days, (fasting) three days of each month, and praying two Rak'ahs before Al-Ghadah (Fajr)."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 2416)"
"6423","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite a great deal of remembrance, engage little in idle talk, make the prayer long and keep the khutbah short, and he would not refrain from walking with a widow or poor person and tending to their needs."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1414)"
"6424","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ used to recite a great deal of remembrance, engage little in idle talk, make the prayer long and keep the khutbah short, and he would not refrain from walking with a widow or poor person and tending to their needs."" (Using translation from Nasāʾī 1414)"
"6425","The people before you used to turn the graves of their prophets and righteous people into places of worship, so do not turn graves into mosques; I forbid you from this."
"6426","I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: ""Your master is the Khalil (close friend) of Allah, the Exalted."
"6427","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) saw Sayyiduna Jibreel (Gabriel), peace be upon him, in his original form; he had 600 wings."
"6428","I saw Jibreel near Sidrat al-Muntaha; he had 600 wings. He had spread one of his wings, from which pearls and rubies of various colors were coming out."
"6429","Ask me and I shall leave no question of yours unanswered for you, and when the people heard about it they were overawed, as if (something tragic) was going to happen. Anas said: I began to look towards the right and the left and (found) that every person was weeping wrapping his head with the cloth. Then a person in the mosque broke the ice and they used to dispute with him by attributing his fatherhood to another man than his own father. He said: Allah's Apostle, who is my father? He said: Your father is Hudhafa. Then 'Umar b. Khattab (Allah be pleased with him) dared say something and said: We are well pleased with Allah as our Lord, with Islam as our code of life and with Muhammad as our Messenger, seeking refuge with Allah from the evil of Turmoil. Thereupon Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: Never did I see the good and evil as today. Paradise and Hell were given a visible shape before me (in this worldly life) and I saw both of them near this well. (Using translation from Muslim 2359e)"
"6430","Sayyiduna Buraidah bin Husaib Aslami (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: Ruqyah is only for the evil eye or fever.\""Then Saeed bin Jubair said: Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) told us the saying of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): \""Various nations were presented before me. I saw a prophet with a few followers, a prophet with one follower, and a prophet with none. Meanwhile, a large group of people passed befor"""
"6431","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with him): One night we were sitting with the Prophet Muhammad (peace and"
"6432","I am also among them."" Then we saw the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) extend his blessed hand forward as if to grasp something, then he went into bowing (ruku‘). After that, he performed the prayer quickly. When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) finished the prayer with salam, he sat down, and we also sat around him. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""I know that the length of my prayer and standing made you anxious."" We said: ""Yes, O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) — we heard you saying: 'O my Lord, I am among them.'"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By Him in Whose hand is my soul, whatever has been promised to you regarding the Hereafter was presented before me during my standing at this place, until even Hell was presented before me. A part of it came towards me, until it came close to this place of mine, so I feared that it might engulf you, so I said: 'O my Lord, I am among these people.' Allah turned it away from you, then its parts turned away like carpets. I looked towards it and saw Amr bin Harithan from the tribe of Ghifar leaning on his bow in Hell. And there was also a woman from Himyar in Hell who was the owner of a cat. She had tied up the cat, neither giving it anything to eat nor letting it go free."
"6433","When we came to the Prophet ﷺ, each one would sit down where there was room. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4825)"
"6434","When the Messenger of Allah ﷺ was distributing something, a man came towards him and bent down on him. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ struck him with a bough and his face was wounded. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said to him: Come and take retaliation. He said: no, I have forgiven, Messenger of Allah!. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4536)"
"6435","I have never seen any person who held the blessed hand of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) let go of his hand, until that person himself would be the one to let go of the blessed hand of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) first."
"6436","""The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never criticized any food. if he liked it, he would eat it, and if not, he would leave it."" (Using translation from Tirmidhī 2031)"
"6437","The Messenger of Allah ﷺ never expressed disapproval of food; if he desired it, he ate it, and if he disliked it, he left it alone. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 3763)"
"6438","narrates: When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would camp at night during a journey, he would make his right hand a pillow. And when he would camp after the morning, he would raise his wrist and place his head on his palm."
"6439","The narrator named Ibn Musher narrated this by taking his beard in his fist."
"6440","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to mend his own shoes, sew his own clothes. He (peace and blessings be upon him) used to do all those household tasks that any person does in his own house."
"6441","As-Sam-u-'Alaikum. A'isha said in response: As-Sam-u-'Alaikum (death be upon you) and curse also, whereupon Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: 'A'isha, verily Allah loves kindness in every matter. She said: Did you bear what they said? Thereupon he said: Did you not hear that I said (to them): Wa 'Alaikum. (Using translation from Muslim 2165a)"
"6442","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) was neither foul-mouthed nor ill-mannered. He (peace be upon him) used to say: The best among you are those who have the best character."
"6443","The Prophet (peace be upon him) possessed the best character. He did not use foul language. He did not behave badly. He did not shout in the marketplace. He did not repay evil with evil, rather he forgave and overlooked."
"6444","The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) never struck anything with his blessed hand, except when he was fighting in the way of Allah (then he attacked the enemies), and the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) never struck his wife or any of his servants."
"6445","I will be your predecessor at the (Kawthar) Pond."
"6446","“I shall reach the Cistern (Haud) before you, and I will boast of your great numbers before the nations, so do not fight one another after I am gone.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3944)"
"6447","“I shall reach the Cistern (Haud) before you, and I will boast of your great numbers before the nations, so do not fight one another after I am gone.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 3944)"
"6448","“The distance between the two ends of my Cistern is like the distance between San’a and Al-Madinah,’ or ‘between Al-Madinah and ‘Amman.’” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4304)"
"6449","The statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him): Soon, some men and some women will come carrying bowls and water skins, and then they will not be able to taste anything from it. By this, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) meant that people belonging to other nations will come, whose forgiveness has already taken place. They will bring bowls so that they may drink from this pond, but they will not be able to drink from it because this pond is reserved for this Ummah. It is not for other nations. It is impossible for any disbeliever or hypocrite to be able to obtain bowls and water skins on the Day of Resurrection, because such people will be driven towards Hell on the Day of Resurrection. We seek Allah's refuge from Hell."
"6450","I hope that Allah Almighty will take me to it, and I will drink from it."
"6451","There would be such a vast distance between the sides of my Cistern as it is between Sana' and Medina. (Using translation from Muslim 2303b)"
"6452","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""My cistern is as large as the distance of a month's journey. Its banks are equal. Its water is whiter than snow, more fragrant than musk. Its vessels are as numerous as the stars in the sky. Whoever drinks from it will never feel thirsty again."
"6453","The Prophet ﷺ said, ""There will be a tank (Lake-Fount) in front of you as large as the distance between Jarba and Adhruh (two towns in Sham). (Using translation from Bukhārī 6577)"
"6454","‘One can see in it (the Cistern) jugs of gold and silver, like the number of stars in the sky.” (Using translation from Ibn Mājah 4305)"
"6455","The narrator states: The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was asked about the width of this Hawd, so he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It is from my place here to (the distance of) Oman. The distance between the two is about a month’s journey or a little less."" The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was asked about the drink of this Hawd, so he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""It will be whiter than milk and sweeter than honey. It will have two channels through which water will come from Paradise. One of them will be made of pearl and the other of gold."
"6456","The narrator states) The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was asked about the width of this Hawd, so he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""From where I am standing to Oman (the distance is as wide as that)."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) was asked about its drink, so he (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Its drink will be whiter than milk and sweeter than honey. This Hawd will have two channels coming from Paradise. One of them will be made of gold and the other of silver."" The narrator named Bandar says: I said to Yahya bin Hammad: Is this the narration transmitted by Abu Awanah? He replied: I heard this narration from Abu Awanah himself. I said: Please check for me the narration transmitted by Shu'bah. He searched for this narration in it and then narrated this hadith."
"6457","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: As much as the distance between Aden and Oman, and it has two spouts, made of gold and silver. He asked: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! What will be the drink of your Hawd like? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: It will be whiter than milk, sweeter than honey in taste, and its fragrance will be purer than musk. Whoever drinks from it will never feel thirsty again, and his face will never become dark. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) In this narration, it is mentioned that its two spouts are made of gold and silver, whereas in the narration we mentioned from Sayyiduna Thawban (may Allah be pleased with him), it is mentioned that its two spouts are made, one of pearl and one of gold. So, there is no contradiction between these two narrations, because one of the two spouts will be made of gold, and as for the other, it is possible that it is made of silver and adorned with pearls. In this way, there remains no contradiction between the two narrations."
"6458","The distance between the two edges of my Hawd (cistern) is as much as the distance from Aylah to Sana'a, which is the distance of one month's journey. The width of this Hawd is equal to its length. There are two channels in it that come from Paradise, made of silver and gold. Its drink (or water) is whiter than milk, sweeter than honey, and colder than ice. By this Hawd, there are as many cups as there are stars in the sky."
"6459","My Cistern would be as extensive as the distance between Aila and San'a, of Yemen, and there would be in it jugs like stars in the sky. (Using translation from Muslim 2303a)"
"6460","I have reserved my specific supplication for the intercession of my ummah on the Day of Resurrection."
"6461","I have postponed my supplication for the intercession of my Ummah in the Hereafter."
"6462","The spoils of war have been made lawful for me, which were not made lawful for anyone before me. I have been helped through awe; the enemy is overcome with fear from a distance of one month's journey. The entire earth has been made a means of purification and a place of prayer for me. And it was said to me: Ask, and you will be given. So I have reserved my supplication for the intercession of my Ummah on the Day of Resurrection. If Allah wills, this supplication will be granted to everyone who does not associate anyone with Allah."
"6463","I woke up and there was no one in front of the camel of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) (i.e., the Prophet was not present). I set out in search of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), and Sayyiduna Mu'adh bin Jabal (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Qais (may Allah be pleased with him) were also standing there. I asked: Where is the Messenger of Allah? They replied: We do not know, but we heard a sound from the upper part of the valley, a sound like that of a millstone turning. The narrator says: Shortly after, the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) came to us. He informed us: A messenger from my Lord came to me and gave me the choice that either half of my Ummah would enter Paradise or I could choose intercession (Shafa'ah), so I chose intercession. The people said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! We beseech you by Allah and by our relationship with you, include us among those who will receive your intercession. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: You will receive my intercession. The narrator says: When those people mounted (their rides), the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I make all those present witnesses that I declare, whoever from my Ummah dies in such a state that he does not associate anyone with Allah, he will receive my intercession."
"6464","I cannot do this. He will mention his mistake which he committed, and because of that mistake he will feel shy before his Lord. He will say: Go to Sayyiduna Nuh (peace be upon him), for he is the first Messenger whom Allah sent. The people will go to Sayyiduna Nuh (peace be upon him). He will say: I cannot do this. He will mention his mistake which he committed, and because of that mistake he will feel shy before his Lord. (He will say:) Go to Sayyiduna Ibrahim (peace be upon him), whom Allah made His Khalil (close friend). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The people will come to Sayyiduna Ibrahim (peace be upon him). He will say: I cannot do this. He will remember his mistake which he committed, and because of that he will feel shy before his Lord. (He will say:) Go to Sayyiduna Musa (peace be upon him), whom Allah created and to whom He gave the Torah. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The people will come to Sayyiduna Musa (peace be upon him). He will say: I cannot do this. He will remember his mistake, because of which he will feel shy before his Lord. (So he will say:) Go to Sayyiduna Isa (peace be upon him). Sayyiduna Isa (peace be upon him) will say: I cannot do this. Go to Sayyiduna Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), who is a servant whose past and future sins Allah has forgiven. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The people will come to me. I will seek permission from my Lord. He will grant me permission, so I will fall into prostration. For as long as Allah wills, I will remain in prostration. Then it will be said: O Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), raise your head. Speak, you will be heard. Ask, you will be given. Intercede, your intercession will be accepted. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I will raise my head and praise my Lord with such words as He will teach me, then I will intercede and a limit will be set for me. I will take those people out of Hell and admit them into Paradise. Then I will return to prostration. For as long as Allah wills, He will let me remain in prostration. Then it will be said: Muhammad, raise your head from prostration. Speak, you will be heard. Ask, you will be given. Intercede, your intercession will be accepted. So I will raise my head and praise my Lord with such words as He will teach me, then I will intercede and a limit will be set for me. I will take those people out of Hell and admit them into Paradise. Then I will return to prostration. For as long as Allah wills, He will let me remain in prostration. Then it will be said: Muhammad! Raise your head from prostration. Speak, you will be heard. Ask, you will be given. Intercede, your intercession will be accepted. So I will raise my head and praise my Lord with such words as He will teach me, then I will intercede and a limit will be set for me. I will take those people out and admit them into Paradise. Then I will place my head (in prostration). For as long as Allah wills, He will let me remain (in prostration). Then it will be said to me: Raise your head (from prostration), speak, you will be heard. Ask, you will be given. Intercede, your intercession will be accepted. So I will raise my head and praise my Lord with such words as He will teach me, then I will intercede and a limit will be set for me. I will take those people out of Hell and admit them into Paradise."" The narrator named Abu Awanah says: I do not know whether the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said this the third or fourth time: I will say: O my Lord, now only those remain in Hell whom the Qur'an (has decreed) to remain (the narrator is unsure, perhaps these are the words) for whom it has been decreed to remain in Hell forever. (Imam Ibn Hibban, may Allah have mercy on him, says:) Hasan bin Sufyan has narrated these words in this narration: ""Go to Sayyiduna Musa (peace be upon him), whom Allah created,"" whereas the original words are: ""with whom Allah spoke."
"6465","The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) liked that part of the goat’s meat the most. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) tore it with his teeth and ate it, and said: On the Day of Resurrection, I will be the leader of all mankind. Then he ate from it a second time and said: On the Day of Resurrection, I will be the leader of all mankind. Then he ate from it a third time and said: On the Day of Resurrection, I will be the leader of all mankind. When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) saw that his companions did not ask him any question, he said: Why do you not ask how this will be? The people said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! How will this be? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: (On the Day of Resurrection) all people will be standing before the Lord of all the worlds. The caller will be able to make his voice reach them. The sight will be able to see them. And the sun will be close to their heads. Its heat will be a cause of severe hardship for them. And the nearness of the sun will be a cause of distress for them. Because of their situation, they will go weeping and wailing and will come to Sayyiduna Adam (peace be upon him). And they will say: O Sayyiduna Adam (peace be upon him), you are the father of mankind. Allah Almighty created you with His own hand of power. He commanded the angels, so they prostrated to you. Intercede for us before your Lord. Do you not see what a terrible situation we are in? Then Sayyiduna Adam (peace be upon him) will say: My Lord is as angry today as He has never been before, and He will never be so angry after this. He commanded me with one thing, but I did not obey Him. Now I fear that He may cast me into Hell. Go to someone else instead of me (now) I am concerned only for myself, only for myself. They will go to Sayyiduna Nuh (peace be upon him) and say: O Sayyiduna Nuh (peace be upon him), you are Allah’s Prophet. You are the first person to be sent as a Messenger. Intercede for us before your Lord. Do you not see what a terrible situation we are in? Sayyiduna Nuh (peace be upon him) will say: My Lord is as angry today as He has never been before, and He will never be so angry after this. I had a supplication which I made against my people, as a result of which they were destroyed. Now I fear that He may cast me into Hell. So go to someone else instead of me. I am concerned only for myself, only for myself. They will go to Sayyiduna Ibrahim (peace be upon him) and say: O Sayyiduna Ibrahim (peace be upon him), you are Allah’s Khalil (close friend). All the inhabitants of the heavens and the earth have heard about your friendship (with Allah). Intercede for us before your Lord. Do you not see what difficulty we are in? Then Sayyiduna Ibrahim (peace be upon him) will say: My Lord is as angry today as He has never been before, and He will never be so angry after this. Then he will mention his statement about the stars: “This is my Lord,” and his statement about their idols: “Rather, the biggest of them did it,” and his statement: “I am sick.” (Then Sayyiduna Ibrahim (peace be upon him) will say:) I fear that He may cast me into Hell. Go to someone else instead of me. I am concerned only for myself, only for myself. They will go to Sayyiduna Musa (peace be upon him) and say: O Sayyiduna Musa (peace be upon him), you are such a Prophet whom Allah Almighty chose for His message. He spoke to you. Intercede for us before your Lord. Do you not see what difficulty we are in? Then Sayyiduna Musa (peace be upon him) will say: My Lord is as angry today as He has never been before, and He will never be so angry after this. I killed a person, although I was not commanded to do so, so I fear that He may admit me into Hell. Go to someone else instead of me. I am concerned only for myself, only for myself. Then they will go to Sayyiduna Isa (peace be upon him) and say: You are Allah’s Prophet, you are His Word, His Spirit which He cast into Sayyiduna Maryam, a spirit coming from Him. Intercede for us before your Lord. Do you not see what difficulty we are in? Then Sayyiduna Isa (peace be upon him) will say: My Lord is as angry today as He has never been before, and He will never be so angry after this. I fear that He may cast me into Hell. Go to someone else instead of me. I am concerned only for myself, only for myself. ‘Umara, the narrator, says: To my knowledge (these words are not in the narration) that he mentioned any sin. Then the people will come to Sayyiduna Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) and say: You (peace and blessings be upon him) are Allah’s Messenger, the Seal of the Prophets. Allah Almighty has forgiven your past and future sins. Intercede for us before your Lord. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) says: I will go from there and come to the Throne. I will fall into prostration before my Lord, so the Lord of all the worlds will grant me such a station in His presence that He has not granted to anyone before me, nor will He grant it to anyone after me. He will say: O Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), admit your Ummah through the right-hand door (of Paradise), those people for whom there will be no reckoning, although they may also enter through other doors with other people. (Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said:) By the One in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, the width of one door of Paradise is as much as the distance between Makkah and Hajar (the narrator is unsure, perhaps these are the words), or as much as the distance between Hajar and Makkah. The narrator says: I do not know which of the two words is mentioned first in the narration."
"6466","The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: By Him in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, I had thought that among my Ummah, you would be the first to ask me about this, because I have noticed that you are very eager to acquire knowledge. By Him in Whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, for me, the people coming one after another to the gates of Paradise is more important than my intercession being completed for them. My intercession will be granted to every person who bears witness with complete sincerity that there is no deity except Allah and that Muhammad (peace be upon him) is the Messenger of Allah. His tongue affirms what is in his heart, and his heart affirms what is on his tongue."
"6467","The Prophet ﷺ said: My intercession will be for those of my people who have committed major sins. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4739)"
"6468","The Prophet ﷺ said: My intercession will be for those of my people who have committed major sins. (Using translation from Abū Dāʾūd 4739)"
"6469","I have reserved my supplication for intercession for my ummah on the Day of Resurrection."
"6470","The narrator says, after a short while, the Prophet (peace be upon him) came to us. He (peace be upon him) said: A messenger from my Lord came to me. He gave me the choice, either half of my Ummah would enter Paradise or I would intercede (no matter how many people it may be), so I chose intercession. We said: O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! We beseech you by Allah and by our companionship with you, include us among those who will receive your intercession. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: You are among those who will receive my intercession. The narrator says: Then we went to the people, and they were anxious. They had found the Prophet (peace be upon him) absent. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: That night a messenger from my Lord came to me, and he gave me the choice that either half of my Ummah would enter Paradise or I would choose intercession, so I chose intercession. The people said: We beseech you by Allah, include us among those who will receive your intercession. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: I make all those present witnesses that my intercession will be granted to every member of my Ummah who dies in such a state that he does not associate anyone with Allah."
"6471","I struck my hand (on its soil), and the fragrance of the soil of Paradise was like musk, and its pebbles were like pearls."
"6472","I entered Paradise and there was a river there. Its banks were made of pearls. I struck my hand on the flow of its water and its fragrance was like musk. I said: O Jibril, what is this? He replied: This is the Kawthar which Allah the Exalted has granted you (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words): that is, your Lord has granted you."
"6473","I entered Paradise and there was a river flowing there, whose water was white like milk and sweeter than honey. On both its banks were tents made of pearls. I touched its soil and it was like musk. I asked Sayyiduna Jibreel (peace be upon him): What is this? He replied: This is the Kawthar which Allah Almighty has granted to you (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"6474","I was walking in Paradise. During this, a river came before me. On both its banks were tents made of hollow pearls. Then the angel who was with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Do you know what this is? This is the Kawthar which your Lord has granted you. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) placed his blessed hand on the ground and lifted its soil, and it was like musk."
"6475","The earth will be split open for me first. I will intercede first, and my intercession will be accepted first.”"
"6476","I am also facing the same situation as you are facing. You people go to your next father after your first father (i.e., go to Sayyiduna Nuh (peace be upon him) because the command of Allah Almighty is): ""Indeed, Allah chose Adam and Nuh and the family of Ibrahim and the family of Imran above the worlds."" So the people will go to Sayyiduna Nuh (peace be upon him) and say: Intercede for us with your Lord, because Allah Almighty chose you. He accepted your supplication, so much so that there was no disbeliever left on earth. So Sayyiduna Nuh (peace be upon him) will say: I cannot do this. You people go to Sayyiduna Ibrahim (peace be upon him) because Allah Almighty made him His friend (Khalil). So the people will come to Sayyiduna Ibrahim (peace be upon him), and he will say: I cannot do this. You people go to Sayyiduna Musa (peace be upon him) because Allah Almighty honored him with His speech. Sayyiduna Musa (peace be upon him) will say: I cannot do this. You people go to Sayyiduna Isa bin Maryam (peace be upon him) because he used to cure the born blind and the leper. He used to bring the dead back to life. Sayyiduna Isa (peace be upon him) will also say: I cannot do this. You people go to the one who is the leader of all the children of Adam. On the Day of Resurrection, the earth will be split open first for him. You people go to Sayyiduna Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) so that he may intercede for you with your Lord. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) says: Those people will come (to me). I will go to Jibril. Jibril will go to his Lord, so Allah Almighty will say: Give him (the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him) permission and give him the glad tidings of Paradise. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) says: Sayyiduna Jibril (peace be upon him) will take the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) along. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) will go into prostration, which will last about a week, then Allah Almighty will say: O Muhammad, raise your head, speak and you will be heard, intercede and your intercession will be accepted. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) will raise his head, and when he sees his Lord, he will again go into prostration, which will last a full week. Allah Almighty will say: O Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), raise your head, speak and you will be heard, intercede and your intercession will be accepted. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) will again go into prostration, so Sayyiduna Jibril (peace be upon him) will hold the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) by his side. At that time, Allah Almighty will inspire the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) with words of supplication, which He has never inspired to any human before. So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) will say: O my Lord! You have made me the leader of all the children of Adam. I am not saying this out of pride. On the Day of Resurrection, the earth will be split open first for me. I am not saying this out of pride, until the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) will come to the Hawd (Pond) of Kawthar on the Day of Resurrection. It is larger than the area between Sana’a and Aylah. Then it will be said: Call the Siddiq (truthful one) so that he may intercede, then it will be said: Call the Prophets, so a Prophet will come, with some people with him, a Prophet will come with five or six people with him, a Prophet will come with no one with him, then it will be said: Call the martyrs so that they may intercede for whomever they wish. When the martyrs have done so, Allah Almighty will say: I am the Most Merciful of those who show mercy. Admit into My Paradise every person who did not associate anyone with Me, so the people will enter Paradise. Then Allah Almighty will say: Look into Hell, is there anyone there who ever did any good? So the angels will find a person in Hell. He will be asked: Did you ever do any good? He will say: No, but I used to deal gently with people when buying and selling. Allah Almighty will say: Be gentle with My servant as he was gentle with My servants. Then another person will be taken out of Hell. He will be asked: Did you ever do any good? He will reply: No, but I instructed my children that when I die, burn me in fire and then crush me until I become like kohl (powder), then scatter me in the river and let the wind carry me away. So Allah Almighty will ask: Why did you do this? He will say: Out of fear of You. So Allah Almighty will say: Look at the greatest kingdom, you are given as much as it and ten times more. The servant will say: Are You mocking me while You are the King? (The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said) At this I laughed at the time of Duha (forenoon). The narrator named Ishaq says: This is the best hadith. This narration has been transmitted by several individuals from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) in a similar manner, among whom are Sayyiduna Hudhayfah, Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud, Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with them), and others. This same narration is also transmitted with another chain of narration."
"6477","Messenger of Allah ﷺ said, ""Noah will be called on the Day of Resurrection and he will say, 'Labbaik and Saʿdaik, O my Lord!' Allah will say, 'Did you convey the Message?' Noah will say, 'Yes.' His nation will then be asked, 'Did he convey the Message to you?' They will say, 'No Warner came to us.' Then Allah will say (to Noah), 'Who will bear witness in your favor?' He will say, 'Muhammad and his followers. So they (i.e. Muslims) will testify that he conveyed the Message. And the Apostle (Muhammad) will be a witness over yourselves, and that is what is meant by the Statement of Allah ""Thus We have made of you a just and the best nation that you may be witnesses over mankind and the Apostle (Muhammad) will be a witness over yourselves."" (2.143) (Using translation from Bukhārī 4487)"
"6478","I will be the leader of all the children of Adam. And I do not say this out of pride. And the earth will be split open for me first, and I will be the first to intercede, and my intercession will be accepted. In my hand will be the 'Banner of Praise.' Sayyiduna Adam (peace be upon him) and everyone else will be under me (that is, under this banner)."
"6479","I and my Ummah will come upon a mound. My Lord will clothe me in a green garment, then whatever Allah wills, I will say at that time (words in praise of Allah). This is the Maqam-e-Mahmood (the Praised Station)."
"6480","The prophets will reply: Each of us is an unlettered prophet. Who among us has been called? He will return a second time and ask: Where is the unlettered Arab prophet? The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Sayyiduna Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) will descend from the pulpit and come to the door of Paradise and knock on it. The gatekeeper will ask from inside: Who is it? You will reply: Muhammad (the narrator is unsure, perhaps these are the words) Ahmad. It will be asked: Has he been called? They will reply: Yes. Then the door will be opened for him. He will enter, and his Lord will manifest Himself before him. Never before has the Lord manifested Himself to any other prophet. Then he will fall into prostration before Allah, and will praise Allah with such words that no one before him nor after him will have praised Allah with those words. It will be said to him: O Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), raise your head, speak and you will be heard, intercede and it will be accepted, ask and it will be granted. He will say: O my Lord, my ummah, my ummah. Then it will be said to him: Take out from (Hell) every person who has faith in his heart equal to the weight of a barley grain. Then he will return and fall into prostration before Allah, and will praise Allah with such words that no one before him has praised Allah with those words, nor will anyone after him. Then it will be said to him: Muhammad, raise your head, speak and you will be heard, intercede and it will be accepted, ask and it will be granted. Then it will be said to him: Take out from Hell every person who has faith in his heart equal to the weight of a wheat grain. Then he will come a third time and fall into prostration before Allah, and will praise Allah with such words that no one before him has praised Allah with those words, nor will anyone after him. Then it will be said to him: Take out from Hell every person who has faith in his heart equal to the weight of a mustard seed. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) will return and fall into prostration, and will praise Allah with such words that no one before him has praised Allah with those words, nor will anyone after him. Then it will be said to him: O Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), raise your head, speak and you will be heard, intercede and it will be accepted, ask and it will be granted. Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) will say: O my Lord, whoever has said La ilaha illallah (there is no god but Allah) (let him also be ordered to come out of Hell). Then it will be said to him: O Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), you have no concern with this; this is exclusively for Me, and today I Myself will reward for it.”"
"6481","I will be the first to knock at the door of Paradise."
"6482","I recognise the stone in Mecca which used to pay me salutations before my advent as a Prophet and I recognise that even now. (Using translation from Muslim 2277)"
"6483","Many a person with disheveled hair and covered with dust is turned away from the doors (whereas he is held in such a high esteem by Allah) that if he were to adjure in the name of Allah (about anything) Allah would fulfil that. (Using translation from Muslim 2622)"
"6484","The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""If you had kept giving, you would have found it."
"6485","I believe in this, Abu Bakr and Umar also believe in this (that the cow can speak), even though these two were not present there.' Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Once a man was taking his goats along. A wolf caught one of the goats. The shepherd went after the wolf and rescued the goat from it. The wolf said: 'What will you do on the day when it will be the day of the beasts' rule? On that day, there will be no guardian of these goats except me.' The people present with the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'Subhan Allah!' The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'I, Abu Bakr, and Umar also believe in this (that the wolf can speak), even though these two were not present there.'"
"6486","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""Once a man rode a cow, so the cow turned towards him and said: I have not been created for this purpose; I have been created for farming.\"" The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: \""I, Abu Bakr, and Umar believe in this.\"" Once a wolf caught a goat. The shepherd chased after it. The wolf said: \""Who will protect it on the day reserved for predators, when there"
"6487","The man said: Subhan Allah, alright. I accept Allah Almighty as a guarantor. The man gave him 600 dinars, and they agreed upon a period. Then the other man boarded a ship with the wealth to trade with it. Allah Almighty had decreed that the specified period would pass, and it did, but the sea was a barrier between the two men. The owner of the wealth would come to the shore and inquire about him. When he asked people about the other man, they would say: We left him at such and such a place. So the owner of the wealth would say: O Allah, You are my guardian in the matter of that man. I gave him that thing on Your guarantee. The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) says: The man who owed the money went, took a piece of wood, placed the wealth inside it, then wrote a note stating: This wealth is from so-and-so to so-and-so. I am entrusting your wealth to my guarantor. Then he sealed the mouth of the wood and threw it into the sea. The wood floated in the sea until it reached the shore. The owner of the wealth came to the shore to inquire about it. There he found the piece of wood, picked it up, and took it home. When he split the wood, he found the dinars and the letter inside. The man took the letter and read it, and realized (that this was indeed his money). Then the other man also arrived. The owner of the wealth asked him about his money. The other man said: I entrusted my wealth to my agent, whom I had made my guarantor. The first man said: Your agent has paid me in full."" Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I remember about myself, we were present with the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) when there was a lot of commotion about which of the two men was more trustworthy."",""Abu Hurairah added"",""""""We often argued and debated among ourselves in the presence of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ about who among us was the most trustworthy."""
"6488","The woman prayed: O Allah, do not let my son die until he becomes like this man (wealthy and prominent). The child said: O Allah, do not make me like him. Then he returned to the breast (and began to nurse again). Then a woman passed by there who was being cursed. The woman prayed: O Allah, do not make my son like this woman. So the child prayed: Then make me like her. As for the rider, he was a disbeliever. As for the woman, people were saying about her that she had committed adultery, but the woman was saying, 'Allah is sufficient for me.' People were saying that she had stolen, but the woman was saying, 'Allah is sufficient for me.'"
"6489","I can put him to trial. They said: Fine, we are ready. She went and offered herself to Jurayj for sin, but Jurayj did not pay attention to her. Then the woman went to a shepherd who used to bring his sheep to Jurayj’s mother. The woman committed sin with the shepherd, then became pregnant and gave birth to a child. She said: This is Jurayj’s child. Because of this, some people from the Children of Israel attacked Jurayj, began to beat him, and started to speak ill of him. They demolished his place of worship. Jurayj asked them: What has happened to you? The people said: You have committed adultery with an immoral woman, and she has given birth to a child. Jurayj asked: Where is the child? The people said: Here he is. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Jurayj performed two units of prayer, then came to the child, touched him with his finger, and said: O child, who is your father? The child said: Such-and-such shepherd. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Then the people began to kiss Jurayj’s head and said: We will build your place of worship with gold. Jurayj said: I do not need that; build it with clay as it was before.” The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Once, there was a child in a woman’s lap whom she was breastfeeding. At that time, a rider passed by her, so the woman prayed: O Allah, make my son like this rider (wealthy and noble). The child left his mother’s breast, turned towards the rider, and looked at him, then said: O Allah, do not make me like this rider. Then a woman passed by who was to be stoned. The woman (i.e., the child’s mother) said: O Allah, do not make my son like this slave woman. The child left his mother, looked at the slave woman, and said: O Allah, make me like this slave woman (a believer and faithful). The woman said: O my son, first a rider passed by, so I said: O Allah, make my son like this rider, but you said: Do not make me like him. Then a slave woman passed by, who was to be stoned, so I said: O Allah, do not make my son like this slave woman, and you said: O Allah, make me like her. The boy said: O my mother, this rider is a tyrant, and this slave woman about whom people say she has stolen, she has not stolen, and people say she has committed adultery, but she has not committed adultery. That woman keeps saying: Allah is sufficient for me."
"6490","narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""There are some servants of Allah such that if they swear an oath by Allah's name, Allah fulfills it for them."
"6491","the sister of Ar-Rubai' Umm Harithah injured a person and they referred the dispute to the Messenger of Allah. The Messenger of Allah said: ""Retaliation, retaliation (Qisas)."" Umm Ar-Rabi said: 'O Messenger of Allah, how could retaliation be carried out against so and so? No, by Allah, retaliation willnever be carried out against her!' The Messenger of Allah said: ""Subhan Allah, O Umm Ar-Rabi'! decreed by Allah."" She said: ""No, by Allah, retaliation will never be carried out against her!"" And she carried on until they accepted Diyah (blood money). He (the prophet) said: ""There are among the slaves of Allah who, if they swear by Allah, Allah fulfills their oath. (Using translation from Nasāʾī 4755)"
"6492","I heard Qatadah narrate a similar hadith."
"6493","The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked for food, and the food was reciting tasbih (glorifying Allah)."
"6494","I not tell you something even more astonishing than this? Between these two rocky grounds (in Madinah Munawwarah), there is Allah's Messenger who is informing people about matters that have passed before."" Then the shepherd brought his goats to Madinah Munawwarah. He made them stand in a corner there and himself went to the service of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). He informed the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) about the conversation with the wolf. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) came out (of his house). He said to the shepherd: ""Stand and tell the people."" He told the people what the wolf had said. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""This shepherd has spoken the truth."" Beware! Among the signs of the Hour is also this: wild beasts will talk to humans. By the One in Whose hand is my soul, the Hour will not be established until wild beasts talk to humans. And a man will converse with his shoe and with the tip of his whip. His thigh will inform him about what his wife did after him."
"6495","The moon was split into two; at that time we were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Mina, until one part of the moon went behind the mountain. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Bear witness, all of you."
"6496","narrates: In the blessed era of the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him), the moon was split into two parts."
"6497","narrates: In the blessed era of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), the moon was split into two in Makkah."
"6498","O Abu Jahl b. Hisham, O Umayya b. Khalaf, O Utba b. Rab'ila, O Shaiba b. Rabi'a, have you not found what your Lord had promised with you to be correct? As for me, I have found the promises of my Lord to be (perfectly) correct. Umar listened to the words of Allah's Apostle ﷺ and said: Messenger of Allah, how do they listen and respond to you? They are dead and their bodies have decayed. Thereupon he (the Holy Prophet) said: By Him in Whose Hand is my life, what I am saying to them, even you cannot hear more distinctly than they, but they lack the power to reply. Then'he commanded that they should be buried in the well of Badr. (Using translation from Muslim 2874)"
"6499","I heard ‘Ali ؓ say: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ sent me, az-Zubair and al-Miqdad, and he said: “Go to the garden of Khakh, where you will find a woman riding a camel with whom there is a letter, and take it from her.” We set out with our horses galloping, until we reached that garden, and there we found the woman. We said: Give us the letter. She said: I do not have any letter. We said: Either you give us the letter or we will remove your clothes. So she brought it out from her braided hair, and we took it and brought it to the Messenger of Allah ﷺ and in it (was written): From Hatib bin Abi Baltaʿah to some of the mushrikeen of Makkah, telling them about some of the plans of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ, The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ʿO Hatib, what is this?ʿ He said: Do not be hasty in judging me, O Messenger of Allah ﷺ. I am a man who was attached to Quraish but I was one of them. The Muhajireen who are with you have relatives who will protect their families in Makkah, and I wanted, as i have no blood ties among them, to do them a favour so that they would protect my family. I did not do it out of kufr or because I apostatized from my religion, or because I approved of Kufr after becoming Muslim. The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ʿHe has told you the truth.ʿ ʿUmar ؓ said: O Messenger of Allah ﷺ, let me strike the neck of this hypocrite. He said: “He was present at Badr, and you do not know, perhaps Allah looked upon the people of Badr and said: ʿDo what you wish, for I have forgiven you.ʿ (Using translation from Aḥmad 600)"
"6500","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with both of them) narrates: Once, he participated in a battle between Makkah and Madinah, and a very strong wind blew upon them, to the extent that saddles began to fall. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: \""This is a sign of the death of a hypocrite.\"" The narrator says: When we returned to Madinah, we found out that on that day, a great hypocrite had died."""
"6501","I wish to go quickly. Whoever among you wishes to go quickly with me, let him do so.” Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out, and when he neared Madinah, he said: “This is Taybah” (the narrator is unsure, perhaps these are the words), “this is Tabah.” When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw Mount Uhud, he said: “This mountain loves us and we love it.” Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Shall I not tell you about the best households among the Ansar?” The people said: “Yes, O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)!” The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “The best household among the Ansar is Banu Najjar. Shall I not tell you about those after them?” The people said: “Yes, O Messenger of Allah.” The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “(After them) Banu Sa’idah and Banu Harith bin Khazraj.”"
"6502","The daughter of the Prophet (peace be upon him), Sayyida Fatima (may Allah be pleased with her), came weeping and presented herself before the Prophet (peace be upon him). She said: These people of your tribe have decided against you that when they see you, they will stand against you and will martyr you. In this way, each one of them will take his share of your blood. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: O my daughter, bring me water for ablution. Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) performed ablution and proceeded to the mosque (near the Sacred House, i.e., the Ka’bah). When those people saw the Prophet (peace be upon him), they said: This is he, this is he. Then they lowered their gazes and their chins stuck to their chests. None of them looked up at the Prophet (peace be upon him), and none of them stood up before him, until the Prophet (peace be upon him) came and stood by them. He took a handful of dust and said: May their faces be disfigured. Then the Prophet (peace be upon him) threw that dust upon them, and whichever pebble from that dust reached any one of them, that person was killed on the day of the Battle of Badr."
"6503","I am Muhammad."
"6504","The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Bring me a goat that has not been mated by a male. So I brought a one-year-old kid. The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) took hold of it, then he passed his hand over its udder and supplicated, until its milk began to flow. Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) brought something to serve the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) milked the goat into that vessel, then he said to Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him): Drink. Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) drank it, then after Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) also drank it. Then the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to the udder: Become dry, so it became dry and returned to its previous state. Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: Then I presented myself to the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). I said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Teach me this speech (the narrator is unsure, perhaps these are the words) or teach me this Qur'an. So the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) passed his hand over my head. The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: You are a boy who has understanding (or who will be taught). The narrator says: I learned seventy surahs from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) himself. No one can compete with me in this matter."
"6505","I say, I will bring them to you; otherwise, I will return to you myself and stay with you."
"6506","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to deliver the Friday sermon while leaning against the trunk of a date-palm tree. When he had a pulpit made and moved towards it, that trunk began to weep. The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) came to it and placed his blessed hand upon it."
"6507","I was present in the mosque at that time. I heard the sound of that piece of wood, as if a child was crying, and it continued to cry until the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) descended and went to it and embraced it (when he embraced it), it became calm. The narrator says: When Hasan al-Basri used to narrate this tradition, he would begin to weep and say: O servants of Allah! A piece of wood weeps out of love for the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), because of the rank and status that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) has in the presence of Allah. So you are even more deserving that you should long to be present in the court of the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"6508","The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) used to deliver the sermon leaning against a tree (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words), a trunk (the narrator is in doubt, perhaps these are the words), a piece of wood (or perhaps these are the words), or something else. When the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) had a pulpit made and stood upon it, that thing began to weep near which (the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, used to deliver the sermon). All the people in the mosque heard its crying sound. Then the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) came to it (the narrator is in doubt), perhaps here he used these words, the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) passed his hand over it (or perhaps these words were used), or the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) held it, so it became calm."
"6509","Sayyiduna Amr bin Ma'adh (may Allah be pleased with him) was cut, the Holy Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) applied his saliva on it, and it was healed."
"6510","narrator says: I was brought to the service of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) applied his saliva to it three times, and after that, I have never felt any pain in it until today."
"6511","The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: She will not be able to see me. The woman came and said: O Abu Bakr, your master has satirized me. Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) said: No, he does not recite poetry. The woman said: You are a truthful man to me, then she left. I said: O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! She did not see you. The Prophet (peace be upon him) said: No, an angel had concealed me from her with his wings."
"6512","I cannot do it. The Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: You will not be able to do it. The narrator says: After that, his (right hand) never reached his mouth again."
"6513","Eat with your right hand. He said: I cannot do that, whereupon he (the Holy Prophet) said: May you not be able to do that. It was vanity that prevented him from doing it, and he could not raise it (the right hand) up to his mouth. (Using translation from Muslim 2021)"
"6514","O, it is you; you have grown young. May you not advance in years! That slave-girl returned to Umm Sulaim weeping. Umm Sulaim said: O daughter, what is the matter with you? She said: Allah's Apostle ﷺ has invoked curse upon me that I should not grow in age and thus I would never grow in age, or she said, in my (length) of life. Umm Sulaim went out wrapping her head-dress hurriedly until she met Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He said to her: Umm Sulaim, what is the matter with you? She said: Allah's Apostle, you invoked curse upon my orphan girl. He said: Umm Sulaim, what is that? She said: She (the orphan girl) states you have cursed her saying that she might not grow in age or grow in life. Messenger of Allah ﷺ smiled and then said: Umm Sulaim, don't you know that I have made this term with my Lord. And the term with my Lord is that I said to Him: 1 am a human being and I am pleased just as a human being is pleased and I lose temper just as a human being loses temper, so for any person from amongst my Ummah whom I curse and he in no way deserves it, let that, O Lord, be made a source of purification and purity and nearness to (Allah) on the Day of Resurrection. (Using translation from Muslim 2603)"
"6515","O Allah, for any believing servant whom I curse make that as a source of nearness to Thee on the Day of Resurrection. (Using translation from Muslim 2601f)"
"6516","O Allah, I make a covenant with Thee against which Thou wouldst never go. I am a human being and thus for a Muslim whom I give any harm or whom I scold or upon whom I invoke curse or whom I beat, make this a source of blessing, purification and nearness to Thee on the Day of Resurrection. (Using translation from Muslim 2601b)"
"6517","The narrator says: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed behind for some task. He met me and asked: What is the matter, why are you walking behind? The narrator says: I replied: No, O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! My camel has become tired, otherwise I intended to walk with the people. The narrator says: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck its back part and scolded it, then said: Mount it. Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) says: After that, I saw myself restraining it to walk with the people (i.e., it was going ahead of the people). The narrator says: Before reaching Madinah, we camped at a place. I intended to go home quickly, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Do not go to your wife at night. Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates: I said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! I have recently married. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asked: Whom did you marry? I replied: A previously married woman. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Why did you not marry a virgin, so that you could play with her and she could play with you? The narrator says: I said: O Messenger of Allah, (my father) Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) passed away (the narrator is unsure if these are the words) or was martyred. He left behind some daughters (among the survivors), so I did not like to bring to them a girl like themselves after marriage. The narrator says: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) remained silent. He did not say: You did well or you did badly. The narrator says: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sell me your camel. The narrator says: I said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! It is already yours. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, rather sell it to me. I said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! It is yours. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No, rather sell it to me. I said: Fine, for one uqiyah of gold (I sell it to you), it is yours. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have taken it; you may ride it to Madinah. When I reached Madinah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him): Give him one uqiyah of gold and give more than one uqiyah. The narrator says: He gave me one uqiyah of gold and one qirat. The narrator says: I resolved that the extra payment given by the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would never be separated from me. The narrator says: It remained with me in a pouch until, at the incident of Harrah, the people of Shaam took it away."
"6518","I went out with Messenger of Allah ﷺ on an expedition, but my camel delayed me. Messenger of Allah ﷺ came to me and said to me: Jabir, I said: Yes. Messenger of Allah, (here I am at your beck and call) He said: What is the matter with you? I said: My camel has delayed me and is tired, so I have lagged behind. He (the Holy Prophet) got down and goaded it with a crooked stick and then said: Mount it. So I mounted and (to my great surprise) I saw it (moving so quickly that) I had to restrain it (from going ahead of) Messenger of Allah ﷺ. He (the Holy Prophet) (in the course of journey said to me): Have you married? I said: Yes. He (again) said: Is it with a virgin or one previously married? I said. With one previously married, whereupon he (again) said: Why not with a young girl with whom you could sport and she could have sported with you? I said: I have sisters, so I preferred to marry a woman who could keep them together (as one family). who could comb them and look after them. He said: You are about to go (to your house), and there you have the enjoyment (of the wife's company). He again said: Do you want to sell your camel? I said: Yes. So he bought it from me for one u'qiya (of silver), Then Messenger of Allah ﷺ arrived (at Medina) and I arrived in the evening. I went to the mosque and found him at the door of the mosque, and said: Is it now that you have arrived? I said: Yes, He said: Leave your camel, and enter (the mosque) and offer two rak'ahs. So I entered and offered two rak'ahs of prayer, and then returned. He (the Holy Prophet) then commanded Bilal to weigh out one 'uqiya (of silver) tor me. Bilal weighed that out for me (lowering the scale of) balance. So I proceeded and as I turned my back he said: Call for me, Jabir. So I was called back, and I said (to myself): He would return me the camel, and nothing was more displeasing to me than this (that after having received the price I should also get the camel). He said: Take your camel and keep its price with you, (also). (Using translation from Muslim 715i)"
"6519","I replied: No. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Sell it to me for one uqiyah. I replied: No. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Sell it to me for one uqiyah, so I sold it to him for one uqiyah. I made the condition in this transaction that I would ride it until I reached my home. When I reached (Madina Munawwara), I presented myself before the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to me: Did you think that I made this transaction with you because of your camel and dirhams? Both of these are yours."
